rules:
- id: rule-workflow-execution-model-compliance
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: 'All runtime-native workflows must conform to the CAS Workflow Execution
    Model: CAS Runner orchestrates, workflows reason, and knowledge providers manage
    access. Workflows must consume supplied context and avoid direct repository discovery.'
  title: Rule Workflow Execution Model Compliance
- compliance:
    enabled: true
  id: rule-pattern-decision-lifecycle-alignment
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Ensures consistent interpretation between pattern maturity (knowledge evolution)
    and decision status (governance lifecycle). Prevents conflation of 'observed'
    patterns with 'approved' architecture.
  title: Rule Pattern Decision Lifecycle Alignment
- id: rule-patterns-born-as-supporting
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: All new patterns must be created as supporting by default and never directly
    as core to ensure validation through evidence before becoming foundational.
  title: Rule Patterns Born As Supporting
- id: rule-do-not-merge-across-architectural-layers
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Patterns must not be merged or consolidated across different architectural
    layers to preserve clarity between governance, execution, and reliability concerns.
  title: Rule Do Not Merge Across Architectural Layers
- id: rule-promotion-requires-evidence
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Pattern promotion to core requires strong evidence, preferably from multiple
    sources, to prevent context-specific patterns from becoming foundational.
  title: Rule Promotion Requires Evidence
- id: rule-architecture-work-authority
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Architecture Work is the authoritative source for planning state; generated
    artifacts like AEM or AID must derive their status from it.
  title: Rule Architecture Work Authority
- compliance:
    enabled: true
  id: rule-decision-schema-must-be-structured
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: All decisions must use the structured YAML decision schema (ADR) rather
    than unstructured text to enable machine processing and consistent rendering.
  title: Rule Decision Schema Must Be Structured
- id: rule-shared-knowledge-workspace
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Projects participate in a shared workspace and must not duplicate global
    governance structures or templates during onboarding.
  title: Rule Shared Knowledge Workspace
- id: rule-language-semantic-contract
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Foundational contract defining terminology for architecture artefacts,
    distinguishing between intent, decision status, and system state.
  title: Rule Language Semantic Contract
- id: rule-heuristic-patterns-require-signals
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: All heuristic-derived patterns must include at least one linked signal
    as evidence to ensure traceability to observed behavior.
  title: Rule Heuristic Patterns Require Signals
- id: rule-precedence-hierarchy
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: 'Defines the resolution model: Global Rules > Project Rules > Prompt Rules.
    Higher precedence rules cannot be overridden by lower ones.'
  title: Rule Precedence Hierarchy
- id: rule-system-proposes-architect-decides
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Maintains human-in-the-loop control; systems propose architectural changes
    while architects must explicitly accept, reject, or defer them.
  title: Rule System Proposes Architect Decides
- id: rule-generated-artifacts-not-authoritative
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Generated governance artifacts are summaries of authoritative source files
    and must not store manual state that would be lost on regeneration.
  title: Rule Generated Artifacts Not Authoritative
- compliance:
    enabled: true
  id: rule-adr-single-source-of-truth
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Architecture Decision Records (ADR) are the sole authoritative source for
    decisions; metadata and AEM maps must be derived from them.
  title: Rule Adr Single Source Of Truth
- id: rule-signal-promotion-criteria
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Signals are promoted to patterns only if they meet mandatory criteria for
    recurrence, system impact, reusability, and stability with supporting evidence.
  title: Rule Signal Promotion Criteria
- id: rule-decisions-must-be-persisted
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: All architectural decisions must be saved as structured ADR files before
    they can be reflected in system maps like the AEM.
  title: Rule Decisions Must Be Persisted
- id: rule-decision-status-drives-stage
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: The lifecycle stage of any item (e.g., DONE) is derived from its ADR status.
    Items not marked 'accepted' cannot be considered finished system state.
  title: Rule Decision Status Drives Stage
- id: rule-aem-consistency-with-decisions
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: The Architecture Evolution Map must accurately reflect and never contradict
    the formal decisions recorded in ADRs.
  title: Rule Aem Consistency With Decisions
- id: rule-core-patterns-must-be-foundational
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Core patterns are restricted to foundational architectural primitives and
    must not include specific strategies or implementation-level details.
  title: Rule Core Patterns Must Be Foundational
summary:
  global_rules: 19
  project_rules: 0
  total_rules: 19
